window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-47b0440a51c2fc92"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"code-review\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">代码审查</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面网址末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可查看文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 ChatGPT 或 Codex 理解代码变更、排查潜在问题，并准备审查反馈。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"pull-request-reviews\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">审查拉取请求</h2> <p>Code Review 插件会显示拉取请求（pull request，简称 PR）的描述、变更文件、评论和检查结果。批准之前，可以用它排查潜在问题。</p> <p>GitHub 代码审查已普遍开放。Code Review 对 GitLab 合并请求的支持仍处于预览阶段。若要在 GitLab 中通过 <code>@codex review</code> 触发云端审查，或启用自动合并请求审查，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e0c9ac1b89ddeeb2\">使用 Codex 审查 GitLab 合并请求</a>。</p> <p>若要通过代码仓库事件触发审查，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">GitHub 集成指南</a>和 <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex Cloud（旧版）环境设置</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>桌面应用内置 Code Review。你可以在已安装的插件中将它固定到应用侧边栏。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"view-a-pull-request\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">查看拉取请求</h3> <ol> <li>在侧边栏中打开 <strong>Code Review</strong>。</li> <li>按提示连接你的代码托管平台账户。该账户必须有权访问你要审查的代码库。</li> <li>从侧边栏选择一个拉取请求，或在搜索框中输入它的链接。</li> <li>在 <strong>Summary</strong> 中查看描述、动态、评论和检查结果；打开 <strong>Changes</strong>，即可对照差异内容查看变更文件和评论。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"find-reviews-that-need-attention\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">找出需要处理的审查</h3> <p>使用个人收件箱查找不同代码库中的 GitHub 拉取请求。选择 <strong>Assigned to me</strong> 查看分配给你的审查请求，选择 <strong>Assigned to my team</strong> 查看分配给团队的请求，或选择 <strong>Authored by me</strong> 返回查看自己创建的变更。先确认审查状态，再打开拉取请求查看反馈和检查结果。</p> <p>若要之后继续处理某项审查，请选择工具栏中的图钉。该拉取请求会显示在侧边栏的 <strong>Pinned</strong> 下。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-changed-files-and-related-pull-requests\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">检查变更文件和相关拉取请求</h3> <p>在 <strong>Changes</strong> 中审查完某个文件后，选择该文件对应的 <strong>Mark as viewed</strong>。再次选择即可清除标记。已查看标记只对当前显示的修订版本有效。</p> <p>如果一组变更拆分在相互依赖的多个拉取请求中，可在 <strong>Summary</strong> 中使用 <strong>Stack</strong> 打开相关拉取请求，并检查其差异、评论和检查结果。Code Review 检测到一组尚未关闭的堆叠式拉取请求时，才会显示此部分。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"read-an-automatic-cloud-review\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">查看自动云端审查</h3> <p>连接 ChatGPT Codex 连接器、授予所需的代码库权限并启用自动审查后，Codex 可以在你打开 GitHub 拉取请求之前先进行审查。评论会同时显示在 GitHub 和 Code Review 中。</p> <p>云端审查无需你创建或管理云端环境。有关连接要求、代码库设置以及通过 <code>@codex review</code> 触发审查的说明，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">在 GitHub 中使用 Codex</a>。</p> <p>请对照差异内容核实审查发现。自动云端审查与您在拉取请求聊天中自行发起的审查彼此独立。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-questions-about-the-change\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">针对变更提问</h3> <p>在拉取请求的聊天中描述预期行为，然后请 Codex 解释或调查这项变更。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>选择 <strong>Review with Codex</strong>，即可在新聊天中开始审查。如果拉取请求显示在已有聊天旁边，也可以直接在该聊天中询问这项变更。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>通过已安装的技能和已连接的数据源，向 Codex 提供团队的审查指南或设计文档。请它总结变更并说明风险，然后核实它引用的上下文和代码。</p> <p>例如，某个拉取请求为问题看板添加了 <strong>Open</strong> 和 <strong>Closed</strong> 筛选器。你希望默认仍选择 <strong>All</strong>，而且没有匹配的问题时应显示空状态：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Walk me through this pull request. Focus on the default filter and what\nhappens when there are no matching issues. All should remain the default.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：请带我了解这个拉取请求。重点检查默认筛选器，以及没有匹配问题时会发生什么；“全部”（All）应继续作为默认选项。</p> </blockquote> <p>要求提供证据：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Show me the code path and tests for the no-matches case. Explain what is\ncovered and what still needs verification.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：请展示“没有匹配项”这一情况对应的代码路径和测试，并说明哪些内容已经覆盖、还有哪些内容需要验证。</p> </blockquote> <p>请根据预期行为检查引用的差异和测试。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>选择一项发现，即可在 <strong>Changes</strong> 中查看解释和相关代码行。决定是否需要修复之前，请结合最新差异、预期行为和测试进行核实。若要停止正在运行的审查，请使用审查聊天。</p> <p><a id=\"customize-your-review\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">自定义审查</h3> <p>选择 <strong>Review with Codex</strong> 旁边的齿轮图标 <strong>Review instructions</strong>。你也可以在 <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Code Review</strong> 中编辑这些说明。</p> <p>你可以为 Codex 指定适用于所有审查的评判标准和报告格式，例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start with a short summary. Prioritize behavior changes, data loss, and\nmissing edge-case tests. For each finding, explain the triggering input,\nexpected behavior, and actual behavior. Use our team's concise review style.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：先写简短摘要。优先检查行为变化、数据丢失和缺少边界情况测试的问题。对每项发现，说明触发问题的输入、预期行为和实际行为，并采用我们团队简洁的审查风格。</p> </blockquote> <p>这些说明适用于你通过 <strong>Review with Codex</strong> 在各个代码库中发起的审查。在审查运行期间所做的修改会从下一次审查开始生效。针对某一项具体变更的问题，请在拉取请求聊天中提出。</p> <p>你也可以选择 <strong>Comic book</strong>、<strong>Visualization</strong> 或 <strong>PDF</strong>，添加一条建议说明，让 Codex 按指定格式解释变更。按需编辑文本，然后选择 <strong>Save</strong> 或 <strong>Run review</strong>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"share-feedback-and-follow-up\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">分享反馈并跟进</h3> <p>在聊天中审查拉取请求，不会自动发布评论、批准或合并该请求。你可以自行选择要分享哪些发现。</p> <p>确认某个问题后，可以请 Codex 帮你起草审查评论：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Using the team review guidelines we discussed, draft a comment describing\nthe no-matches behavior we verified, what should happen instead, and the test\nthat would cover it. Keep the comment as a draft.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：根据我们讨论过的团队审查指南，起草一条评论，说明已经核实的“没有匹配项”行为、实际应有的行为，以及可以覆盖此问题的测试。请保留为草稿。</p> </blockquote> <p>发布前请核对草稿中引用的文件和代码行。在准备好之前，请将草稿留在聊天中：在 <strong>Summary</strong> 或 <strong>Changes</strong> 中发布评论会立即将其发送给代码托管平台，不会等待你选择 <strong>Submit review</strong>。</p> <p>使用 <strong>Submit review</strong> 选择 <strong>Comment</strong>、<strong>Approve</strong> 或 <strong>Request changes</strong>，并将审查结果发送给代码托管平台。提交前请核对所选决定和审查评论。</p> <p>如果你是作者，请返回拉取请求并请 Codex 处理具体反馈。检查修改结果并运行相关测试。批准或合并之前，请核对最新修订版本、检查结果和待处理反馈。</p> <p>Code Review 不支持编辑附有图片的拉取请求描述。如需编辑，请在 GitHub 中打开该拉取请求。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"continue-in-a-chat\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">在聊天中继续处理</h3> <p>如果 <strong>Summary</strong> 中显示 <strong>Threads</strong>，选择其中一个关联聊天即可返回对应对话。这些是与你的拉取请求关联的聊天。</p> <p>在 Codex 中，打开尚未关闭的拉取请求，在 <strong>Checks</strong> 中选择 <strong>Fix</strong>，即可将失败的检查附加到聊天中。系统会准备一条消息，但不会自动发送。检查或补充提示词，然后发送消息请 Codex 调查。推送修复前，请检查修改结果并重新运行相关测试。</p> <p>可用的诊断信息取决于检查服务提供方。对于第三方持续集成（CI），Codex 可以使用报告到 GitHub 的状态和输出。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-review\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"review-local-changes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">审查本地变更</h2> <p>Codex 内置的 <code>/review</code> 命令用于审查 Git 工作副本中的变更；Code Review 插件则用于审查拉取请求。 请选择你使用的客户端，查看相应操作步骤。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT Work 中，上传需要审查的代码，或通过已安装的源代码<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>提供代码。在提示词中说明拉取请求、分支、提交、文件和审查标准。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"review-in-the-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">在桌面应用中审查</h3> <p>打开审查面板，了解变更内容，针对具体代码行提供反馈，并决定要暂存、撤销、提交或推送哪些更改。</p> <p>若要请 Codex 审查变更，请在消息输入框中键入 <code>/review</code>。选择 <strong>Review against a base branch</strong> 或 <strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong>。Codex 会按优先级报告发现的问题，但不会更改你的工作树。</p> <p>审查面板要求项目位于 Git 代码库中。如果项目尚未纳入 Git 代码库，应用会提示你创建一个。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>键入 <code>/review</code> 可打开 CLI 审查预设。Codex 会启动专用审查器，读取选定的差异，并按优先级报告可执行的发现，但不会更改你的工作树。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 IDE 扩展的消息输入框中键入 <code>/review</code>。选择 <strong>Review against a base branch</strong> 或 <strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong>。Codex 会按优先级报告发现的问题，但不会更改你的工作树。</p> <p>只有当打开的项目位于 Git 代码库中时，才会显示 <code>/review</code> 命令。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-review-scope\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">选择审查范围</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在提示词中指出要检查的拉取请求、分支、提交或文件。若要审查无法通过已安装的源代码插件访问的本地文件，请将其上传到聊天中。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"what-changes-it-shows\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">面板会显示哪些变更</h3> <p>审查面板反映的是 Git 代码库的当前状态，而不只是 Codex 修改的内容。其中包括 Codex 所做的变更、你自己所做的变更，以及代码库中其他尚未提交的变更。</p> <p>默认情况下，审查面板显示 <strong>Unstaged</strong> 变更。选择 <strong>Staged</strong> 查看 Git 暂存区中的内容，选择 <strong>Commit</strong> 查看指定提交，选择 <strong>Branch</strong> 查看与基准分支之间的差异，或选择 <strong>Last turn</strong> 查看助手最近一轮所做的变更。</p> <p><a id=\"review-multiple-repositories\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_15\">审查多个代码库</h3> <p>当<a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76?anchor=use-local-projects-for-folders-and-codebases\">本地项目包含多个文件夹</a>，且这些文件夹分别由不同的 Git 代码库管理时，审查面板可以显示每个代码库中的变更。打开审查面板顶部的代码库选择器，即可切换查看其他代码库中的改动行，无需离开当前面板。</p> <p>选择 <strong>Last turn</strong> 可查看助手最近一轮在所有已附加代码库中的变更。此视图下，代码库选择器会显示 <strong>All repos</strong>。其他审查范围（如 <strong>Unstaged</strong>、<strong>Staged</strong> 和 <strong>Branch</strong>）仅适用于你选中的代码库。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>可选择以下一种 <code>/review</code> 审查范围：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Review against a base branch</strong>：查找合并基点，并审查当前分支相对于基准分支的差异。</li> <li><strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong>：包括已暂存、未暂存和未跟踪的文件。</li> <li><strong>Review a commit</strong>：审查指定提交对应的确切变更集。</li> <li><strong>Custom review instructions</strong>：根据你提供的标准重点开展审查。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>可选择以下一种 <code>/review</code> 审查范围：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Review against a base branch</strong>：将当前分支与所选分支进行比较。</li> <li><strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong>：审查工作树中的变更。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"work-with-review-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_16\">处理审查结果</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>审查发现会显示在网页聊天中。你可以要求提供证据、请求进一步缩小范围进行审查，或请 ChatGPT 准备修改后的文件。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"code-review-results\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_17\">代码审查结果</h3> <p>审查发现会以行内评论的形式显示在审查面板中。</p> <p>默认情况下，审查会在当前聊天中运行。前往 <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>General</strong> &gt; <strong>Code review</strong>，选择 <strong>Detached</strong> 可另开一个审查聊天。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f?sectionMissing=app-code-review\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">开发者设置（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：审查面板中显示的代码行内评论</p> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>审查结果会作为一轮内容显示在对话记录中。如果希望审查使用的模型不同于当前会话模型，请在 <code>config.toml</code> 中设置 <code>review_model</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>默认情况下，审查会在当前聊天中运行。如果希望 <code>/review</code> 单独开启一个审查聊天，请将 <code>chatgpt.reviewDelivery</code> 设为 <code>detached</code>。请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f?sectionMissing=ide-editor-settings-reference\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">IDE 扩展设置参考（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>即使你请 ChatGPT 准备修改后的文件，该聊天仍受其可用工具和工作区权限限制。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>如果你请 Codex 应用它发现的问题修复，仍会遵循常规的<a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">沙箱和审批设置</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"navigating-the-review-pane\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_18\">浏览审查面板</h2> <ul> <li>单击文件名通常会在你选择的编辑器中打开该文件。你可以在<a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f?sectionMissing=app-project-and-terminal-behavior\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">开发者设置（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>中选择默认编辑器。</li> <li>单击文件名所在行的空白处可展开或折叠差异。</li> <li>按住 <kbd>Command</kbd> 的同时单击某一代码行，可在你选择的编辑器中打开该行。</li> <li>如果你认可某项变更，可以<a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92?anchor=staging-and-reverting-files\">暂存该变更，或撤销不需要的更改</a>。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"inline-comments-for-feedback\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_19\">使用行内评论反馈</h2> <p>行内评论可让你直接针对差异中的具体代码行提供反馈。这通常是引导 Codex 正确修复问题的最快方式。</p> <p>添加行内评论：</p> <ol> <li>打开审查面板。</li> <li>将指针悬停在要评论的代码行上。</li> <li>选择出现的 <strong>+</strong> 按钮。</li> <li>输入反馈并提交。</li> <li>完成反馈后，向聊天发送一条消息。</li> </ol> <p>由于评论针对具体代码行，Codex 能够比处理一般性指令时更准确地作出回应。</p> <p>Codex 会将行内评论视为审查指导。添加评论后，请再发送一条消息，明确说明你的意图，例如：“处理这些行内评论，并尽量缩小改动范围。”</p> <p><a id=\"staging-and-reverting-files\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_20\">暂存与撤销文件</h2> <p>审查面板提供 Git 操作，方便你在提交前整理差异内容。</p> <p>你可以在以下层级暂存、取消暂存或撤销变更：</p> <ul> <li><strong>整个差异</strong>：使用审查面板顶部的操作按钮，例如 <strong>Stage all</strong> 或 <strong>Revert all</strong>。</li> <li><strong>单个文件</strong>：对单个文件暂存、取消暂存或撤销变更。</li> <li><strong>单个差异块</strong>：对一个差异块暂存、取消暂存或撤销变更。</li> </ul> <p>如果只想保留部分工作，请使用暂存；如果想丢弃某些变更，请使用撤销。</p> <p><a id=\"staged-and-unstaged-states\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_21\">已暂存与未暂存状态</h3> <p>Git 可以在同一个文件中同时保存已暂存和未暂存的变更。因此，审查面板可能会在两个视图中都显示同一个文件。这是 Git 的正常行为。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"code-review\">Code review</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use ChatGPT or Codex to understand code changes, investigate potential issues, and prepare review feedback.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"pull-request-reviews\">Pull request reviews</h2> <p>The Code Review plugin shows a pull request's description, changed files, comments, and checks. Use it to investigate potential issues before approving.</p> <p>GitHub code review is generally available. GitLab merge request support in Code Review is in preview. To trigger cloud reviews from GitLab with <code>@codex review</code> or automatic merge request reviews, see <a href=\"#/article/a-e0c9ac1b89ddeeb2\">Review GitLab merge requests with Codex</a>.</p> <p>For repository-triggered reviews, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">GitHub integration guide</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex Cloud (Legacy) environment setup</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The desktop app includes Code Review. You can pin it to the app sidebar from your installed plugins.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"view-a-pull-request\">View a pull request</h3> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Code Review</strong> from the sidebar.</li> <li>Connect your source account when prompted. Use an account with access to the repository you want to review.</li> <li>Select a pull request from the sidebar, or enter its link in the search field.</li> <li>Read <strong>Summary</strong> for the description, activity, comments, and checks. Open <strong>Changes</strong> to inspect changed files and comments alongside the diff.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"find-reviews-that-need-attention\">Find reviews that need attention</h3> <p>Use your personal inbox to find GitHub pull requests across repositories. Choose <strong>Assigned to me</strong> for reviews requested from you, <strong>Assigned to my team</strong> for team requests, or <strong>Authored by me</strong> to return to your own changes. Check the review status, then open the pull request to inspect feedback and checks.</p> <p>To return to a review later, select the pin in its toolbar. The pull request appears under <strong>Pinned</strong> in the sidebar.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-changed-files-and-related-pull-requests\">Inspect changed files and related pull requests</h3> <p>In <strong>Changes</strong>, select <strong>Mark as viewed</strong> on a file after reviewing it. Select the control again to clear the marker. Viewed markers apply to the displayed revision.</p> <p>For changes split across dependent pull requests, use <strong>Stack</strong> in <strong>Summary</strong> to open a related pull request and inspect its diff, comments, and checks. This section appears when Code Review finds a stack of open pull requests.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"read-an-automatic-cloud-review\">Read an automatic cloud review</h3> <p>With the ChatGPT Codex connector, required repository permissions, and automatic reviews enabled, Codex can review a GitHub pull request before you open it. Comments appear on GitHub and in Code Review.</p> <p>Cloud review doesn't require you to create or manage a cloud environment. For connection requirements, repository settings, and reviews triggered with <code>@codex review</code>, see <a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">Use Codex in GitHub</a>.</p> <p>Check the review findings against the diff. Automatic cloud reviews are separate from reviews you start in the pull request's chat.</p> <h3 id=\"ask-questions-about-the-change\">Ask questions about the change</h3> <p>In the pull request's chat, describe the expected behavior and ask Codex to explain or investigate the change.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Select <strong>Review with Codex</strong> to start a review in a new chat. If you're viewing the pull request beside an existing chat, use that chat to ask about the change.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Use installed skills and connected sources to give Codex your team's review guidelines or design documents. Ask it to summarize the change and explain the risks, then verify the context and code it references.</p> <p>For example, a pull request adds <strong>Open</strong> and <strong>Closed</strong> filters to an issue board. You expect <strong>All</strong> to remain the default and an empty state when no issues match:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Walk me through this pull request. Focus on the default filter and what\nhappens when there are no matching issues. All should remain the default.\n</code></pre> <p>Ask for evidence:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Show me the code path and tests for the no-matches case. Explain what is\ncovered and what still needs verification.\n</code></pre> <p>Check the referenced diff and tests against the expected behavior.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Select a finding to inspect its explanation and relevant lines in <strong>Changes</strong>. Check it against the latest diff, expected behavior, and tests before deciding it needs a fix. Use the review chat to stop a running review.</p> <h3 id=\"customize-your-review\">Customize your review</h3> <p>Select the <strong>Review instructions</strong> gear next to <strong>Review with Codex</strong>. You can also edit these instructions in <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Code Review</strong>.</p> <p>Give Codex criteria and a reporting format that apply across your reviews, for example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start with a short summary. Prioritize behavior changes, data loss, and\nmissing edge-case tests. For each finding, explain the triggering input,\nexpected behavior, and actual behavior. Use our team's concise review style.\n</code></pre> <p>These instructions apply to reviews you start with <strong>Review with Codex</strong> across repositories. Changes made during a running review apply to your next review. Use the pull request chat for questions specific to one change.</p> <p>Optionally, select <strong>Comic book</strong>, <strong>Visualization</strong>, or <strong>PDF</strong> to add a suggested instruction for explaining the change in that format. Edit the text as needed, then select <strong>Save</strong> or <strong>Run review</strong>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"share-feedback-and-follow-up\">Share feedback and follow up</h3> <p>Reviewing a pull request in chat doesn't post comments, approve it, or merge it. You choose which findings to share.</p> <p>Once you've verified a concern, ask Codex to help prepare a review comment:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Using the team review guidelines we discussed, draft a comment describing\nthe no-matches behavior we verified, what should happen instead, and the test\nthat would cover it. Keep the comment as a draft.\n</code></pre> <p>Check the draft's file and line references before posting. Keep drafts in chat until you're ready: posting in <strong>Summary</strong> or <strong>Changes</strong> sends the comment to the source provider immediately, without waiting for <strong>Submit review</strong>.</p> <p>Use <strong>Submit review</strong> to choose <strong>Comment</strong>, <strong>Approve</strong>, or <strong>Request changes</strong> and send your review to the source provider. Check the selected decision and review comment before submitting.</p> <p>If you're the author, return to your pull request and ask Codex to address specific feedback. Inspect the resulting changes and run the relevant tests. Before approving or merging, check the latest revision, checks, and outstanding feedback.</p> <p>Editing pull request descriptions with attached images isn't supported in Code Review. Open the pull request in GitHub to edit those descriptions.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"continue-in-a-chat\">Continue in a chat</h3> <p>When <strong>Summary</strong> shows <strong>Threads</strong>, select a linked chat to return to that conversation. These are your chats associated with the pull request.</p> <p>In Codex, select <strong>Fix</strong> in <strong>Checks</strong> on an open pull request to attach failing checks to the chat. This prepares a message without sending it. Review or add your prompt, then send it to ask Codex to investigate. Inspect the resulting changes and rerun the relevant tests before pushing a fix.</p> <p>Available diagnostics depend on the check provider. For third-party CI, Codex can use the status and output reported to GitHub.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"review-local-changes\">Review local changes</h2> <p>Codex's built-in <code>/review</code> command reviews changes in your Git checkout, while the Code Review plugin works with pull requests. Choose your client for the steps that apply.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In ChatGPT Work, upload the code you want reviewed or make it available through an installed source <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugin</a>. In your prompt, identify the pull request, branch, commit, files, and review criteria.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"review-in-the-app\">Review in the app</h3> <p>Open the review pane to understand what changed, give line-specific feedback, and decide what to stage, revert, commit, or push.</p> <p>To ask Codex to review the changes, type <code>/review</code> in the composer. Choose <strong>Review against a base branch</strong> or <strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong>. Codex reports prioritized findings without changing your working tree.</p> <p>The review pane requires a project inside a Git repository. If your project isn't a Git repository yet, the app prompts you to create one.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Type <code>/review</code> to open the CLI review presets. Codex starts a dedicated reviewer that reads the selected diff and reports prioritized, actionable findings without changing your working tree.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Type <code>/review</code> in the IDE extension composer. Choose <strong>Review against a base branch</strong> or <strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong>. Codex reports prioritized findings without changing your working tree.</p> <p>The <code>/review</code> command appears only when the open project is inside a Git repository.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-review-scope\">Choose a review scope</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Name the pull request, branch, commit, or files to inspect in your prompt. To review local files that aren't available through an installed source plugin, upload them to the chat.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"what-changes-it-shows\">What changes it shows</h3> <p>The review pane reflects the state of your Git repository, not just what Codex edited. It includes changes made by Codex, changes you made yourself, and any other uncommitted changes in the repository.</p> <p>By default, the review pane shows <strong>Unstaged</strong> changes. Use <strong>Staged</strong> for the Git index, <strong>Commit</strong> for a selected commit, <strong>Branch</strong> for the diff against your base branch, or <strong>Last turn</strong> for the most recent assistant turn.</p> <h3 id=\"review-multiple-repositories\">Review multiple repositories</h3> <p>When a <a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76?anchor=use-local-projects-for-folders-and-codebases\">local project includes multiple folders</a> backed by different Git repositories, the review pane can show changes from each repository. Open the repository selector in the review header to inspect another repository and see the lines added or removed without leaving the current review pane.</p> <p>Choose <strong>Last turn</strong> to see the assistant's latest changes across the attached repositories. The repository selector shows <strong>All repos</strong> for that view. Other review scopes, such as <strong>Unstaged</strong>, <strong>Staged</strong>, and <strong>Branch</strong>, apply to the repository you select.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Choose one of these <code>/review</code> scopes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Review against a base branch</strong> finds the merge base and reviews your branch diff.</li> <li><strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong> includes staged, unstaged, and untracked files.</li> <li><strong>Review a commit</strong> reviews the exact change set for a selected commit.</li> <li><strong>Custom review instructions</strong> focuses the review on criteria you provide.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Choose one of these <code>/review</code> scopes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Review against a base branch</strong> compares your current branch with a branch you select.</li> <li><strong>Review uncommitted changes</strong> reviews the changes in your working tree.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"work-with-review-results\">Work with review results</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Review findings appear in the web chat. Ask for evidence, request a narrower follow-up review, or ask ChatGPT to prepare revised files.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"code-review-results\">Code review results</h3> <p>Review findings appear as inline comments in the review pane.</p> <p>Reviews run in the current chat by default. Under <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>General</strong> &gt; <strong>Code review</strong>, choose <strong>Detached</strong> to start a separate review chat. See <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f?sectionMissing=app-code-review\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">developer settings (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Inline code review comments displayed in the review pane</p> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The review appears as a turn in the transcript. Set <code>review_model</code> in <code>config.toml</code> when you want reviews to use a different model from the current session.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>By default, the review runs in the current chat. Set <code>chatgpt.reviewDelivery</code> to <code>detached</code> when you want <code>/review</code> to start a separate review chat. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f?sectionMissing=ide-editor-settings-reference\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">IDE extension settings reference (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>If you ask ChatGPT to prepare revised files, the tools and workspace permissions available to the chat still apply.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>If you ask Codex to apply the fixes it finds, your normal <a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">sandbox and approval settings</a> apply.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"navigating-the-review-pane\">Navigating the review pane</h2> <ul> <li>Clicking a file name typically opens that file in your chosen editor. You can choose the default editor in <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f?sectionMissing=app-project-and-terminal-behavior\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">developer settings (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-7969ca0198aaf47f\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>.</li> <li>Clicking the file name background expands or collapses the diff.</li> <li>Clicking a single line while holding <kbd>Command</kbd> pressed opens the line in your chosen editor.</li> <li>If you're happy with a change, you can <a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92?anchor=staging-and-reverting-files\">stage it or revert changes</a> you don't want.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"inline-comments-for-feedback\">Inline comments for feedback</h2> <p>Inline comments let you attach feedback directly to specific lines in the diff. This is often the fastest way to guide Codex to the right fix.</p> <p>To leave an inline comment:</p> <ol> <li>Open the review pane.</li> <li>Hover over the line you want to comment on.</li> <li>Select the <strong>+</strong> button that appears.</li> <li>Write your feedback and submit it.</li> <li>After you finish leaving feedback, send a message back to the chat.</li> </ol> <p>Because comments are line-specific, Codex can respond more precisely than with a general instruction.</p> <p>Codex treats inline comments as review guidance. After leaving comments, send a follow-up message that makes your intent explicit, for example, “Address the inline comments and keep the scope minimal.”</p> <h2 id=\"staging-and-reverting-files\">Staging and reverting files</h2> <p>The review pane includes Git actions so you can shape the diff before you commit.</p> <p>You can stage, unstage, or revert changes at these levels:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Entire diff</strong>: Use the action buttons in the review header, such as <strong>Stage all</strong> or <strong>Revert all</strong>.</li> <li><strong>Per file</strong>: Stage, unstage, or revert an individual file.</li> <li><strong>Per hunk</strong>: Stage, unstage, or revert a single hunk.</li> </ul> <p>Use staging when you want to accept part of the work, and revert when you want to discard it.</p> <h3 id=\"staged-and-unstaged-states\">Staged and unstaged states</h3> <p>Git can represent both staged and unstaged changes in the same file. When that happens, the pane can show the same file in both views. That's normal Git behavior.</p>"};
